## Retry transient SEA transport errors on Lakehouse/RT warehouses

Context: In KG → Explorer against a domain whose Delta graph store is pointed at
a serverless "Lakehouse/RT" SQL warehouse, the UI showed `Error: Error querying
graph` (`GET /dtwin/sync/stats` and `POST /dtwin/sync/filter` → 502). Root cause:
the RT warehouse rejects Thrift and is driven over the Statement Execution API
(SEA); while the serverless warehouse cold-starts/auto-scales, the SEA endpoint
briefly returns `HTTP 500` ("SEA HTTP request failed with status 500").
`SQLWarehouse.execute_query()` / `execute_statement()` had no retry — a single
transient 500 was raised straight through and surfaced as `502 Error querying
graph`. The warehouse self-heals within ~10–25s (a manual refresh worked), but
the first interaction after an idle warehouse always failed.

This change adds a bounded retry-with-reconnect around the borrow+execute path.
Only transient transport/warehouse failures are retried (SEA 5xx, connection
reset/broken pipe, service-unavailable, recycled session/cursor); genuine SQL
errors (`ServerOperationError`: BAD_REQUEST, syntax, permissions) and the RT
"not supported for Thrift protocol" config error are never retried and surface
immediately with their original message. `iter_rows()` (build-pipeline streaming)
is intentionally left unchanged — retrying a partially-yielded generator is
unsafe, and builds run against an already-warm warehouse.

Changes:
1. src/back/core/databricks/SQLWarehouse.py
   Added module-level retry policy (`_SQL_MAX_ATTEMPTS=3`,
   `_SQL_RETRY_BACKOFF_S=(1.5, 4.0)`), marker lists, and a pure
   `_is_retryable_transport_error(exc)` classifier. Added the
   `_run_with_retry(work, *, op)` helper (borrow → run → reconnect on transient
   failure with backoff). Refactored `execute_query()` and `execute_statement()`
   to run their work through it. Guarded the `SET STATEMENT_TIMEOUT = 0` reset in
   `execute_query()` so a failed query on a broken connection no longer masks the
   real error.
2. tests/units/core/test_sql_warehouse.py
   Added `TestRetryClassifier` (SEA 5xx / service-unavailable / connection-reset
   retryable; `ServerOperationError`, Thrift-not-supported, plain SQL errors not
   retryable), `TestExecuteQueryRetry` (transient-then-success, no-retry on SQL
   error, give-up after max attempts), and `TestExecuteStatementRetry`. `time.sleep`
   is patched so the backoff adds no wall-clock time.

